{"name":"Integra","hex":"#405e95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Integra Air","blocks":[{"text":"Integra Air offered chartered and scheduled flight services, as well as air ambulance medevac services, out of Calgary, Alberta, Canada. The airline ceased operations on August 31, 2018, stating that it was undergoing corporate restructuring. The closure also shut down operations of the air ambulance services."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/C-FZVY_Jetsream_J-32_Integra_Air_YVR_24AUG05_%286854883856%29.jpg/330px-C-FZVY_Jetsream_J-32_Integra_Air_YVR_24AUG05_%286854883856%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integra_Air","wikidata":"Q4041440"},{"title":"Integra Bank","blocks":[{"text":"Integra Bank Corporation was the parent of Integra Bank National Association, a retail bank headquartered in Evansville, Indiana, that failed on July 29, 2011. As of March 31, 2010, Integra Bank had $2.9 billion in total assets and operated 67 banking centers and 116 ATMs at locations in Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, and Ohio. The Second Renaissance Revival building was constructed in 1913, and originally housed the National City Bank."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Integra_Bank_on_Main_in_Evansville.jpg/330px-Integra_Bank_on_Main_in_Evansville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integra_Bank","wikidata":"Q6042611"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"20131003 Schoeningen Palaeon DSC08394 PtrQs","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg/500px-20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg","share":0.23875},{"title":"Hazy blue hour in Grand Can